  "convention": "Board x is linear in longitude across the board's bounds; board y is linear in Web Mercator between the bounds' north (y=0) and south (y=1) edges. Board space is unbounded: points outside 0..1 are legal and are what a phone panned off the fence produces.",
  "excluded": "Degenerate bounds (a zero longitude or Mercator span) are deliberately absent: the TypeScript copy clamps the span to 1e-6 while the Swift copy special-cases zero to 0, so the two disagree there. Pick one before adding such a row.",
